{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_558386156#12_1321993795","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage is from a dedicated article on Twitter's financial/ad-business problems and directly explains that Twitter lacked sufficient audience data for advertisers, while social marketers found ROI difficult to estimate, weakening Twitter's ad business despite a favorable election news cycle.","learned":"Twitter's ad revenue declined partly because advertisers lacked adequate information and ROI measurement; Twitter's MAU metric omitted non-logged-in visitors, making its real audience harder to monetize."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3160","reason":"The current query is producing directly relevant segments on advertiser-information and ROI-measurement problems, so continue for more grade-3 evidence from the same or related documents."}}
